@startuml federation-flow
!include ../../datum-theme-sequence.puml

title Location Federation - how a location reaches the cell that is it

actor "Fleet Ops" as ops
actor "Service operator" as svcop
participant "Milo platform\ncontrol plane" as milo
participant "NSO manager\n(location publisher)" as pub <<new>>
participant "services-controller\n-manager" as scm
participant "Project control plane" as project
participant "Karmada hub" as hub
participant "karmada-agent\n(on the cell)" as agent
participant "Edge cell" as cell
participant "compute-manager\n(on the cell)" as ccell

== Prerequisite: the cell declares what it is ==

ops -> hub: label Cluster\ntopology.datum.net/location=us-west-1-alice
note right of hub
  Set at cell registration, so this
  carries a re-registration per cell.
  A cell claims its location; the
  location never names its cell.
end note

ops -> cell: install ServingLocation CRD\n(NSO downstream bundle)
note right of cell
  Must land before any Work selects
  the kind. Otherwise the Work sits
  not-applied, indistinguishable from
  a stalled agent unless the reason
  string is surfaced.
end note

== Identity leg: publishing ==

ops -> milo: create Location us-west-1-alice\n(hand-authored, hand-marked Ready)
milo --> pub: watch event

pub -> pub: validate source

alt city code missing
    pub -> pub: report linkage mismatch,\npublish nothing
else valid
    pub -> hub: apply ServingLocation/us-west-1-alice\n(server-side apply, own field manager)
    pub -> hub: apply ClusterPropagationPolicy\n/location-us-west-1-alice
end

note over pub
  Gated on the Location EXISTING,
  not on it being healthy. An unhealthy
  location is still a real place whose
  workloads need to know where they are.
end note

== Delivery ==

hub -> hub: ResourceBinding resolves clusterAffinity\nagainst the location label

alt no cell carries the label
    hub -> hub: resolves to 0 clusters
    note right of hub
      Published but undeliverable.
      A readable state, not a silence.
    end note
else exactly one cell carries it
    hub -> hub: create Work for that cell
    agent -> hub: pull Work (agent-initiated, pull mode)
    agent -> cell: apply ServingLocation
    agent --> hub: report applied
    hub -> hub: aggregate into ResourceBinding status
end

== Consumption at the cell ==

ccell -> cell: watch ServingLocation

alt exactly one present
    ccell -> ccell: identity = that location
else none delivered, or more than one
    ccell -> ccell: fall back to configured location
    note right of ccell
      Never guess. With neither, report
      the waiting state on the objects
      that are stuck and heal on arrival.
    end note
end

== Availability leg: existing, and independent of the above ==

svcop -> milo: create ServiceAvailability\n(service, location)
milo --> scm: watch event
scm -> scm: evaluate gates: Service Published,\nLocation Ready, class supported
scm -> project: write LocationBinding\nper entitled project

note right of project
  Entitlement is evaluated here and
  never leaves. Nothing at the hub or
  on a cell may re-answer it.
end note

== Where the two legs meet ==

project -> hub: WorkloadDeployment federated\n(compute's own per-city policy)
hub -> cell: WorkloadDeployment
cell --> ccell: reconcile
ccell -> ccell: resolve spec.cityCode against the\nServingLocation delivered by the identity leg
ccell -> ccell: set Status.Location,\nthen Instance.Spec.Location

note over ccell
  Placement decided the cell.
  Identity told the cell what it is.
  Neither leg answers the other's question.
end note

@enduml
